"] [99 1 "// auxiliary vector (AT_PAGESZ, AT_RANDOM); the environment's address and argv[0]'s."] [125 1 "// cFunc is the C program's function named s when it defines one (code, or a native ci has)."] [137 1 "// cResolve is the C function a static foreign call of s calls when the C program has it and hsi's table does not, or"] [138 1 "// it is one of cFirst's."] [146 1 "// cFuncAt is the C program's function at address a, or nil."] [158 1 "// cCall calls f with the machine's argument values (an integer kind or an address as an integer, a float or a double as"] [159 1 "// a floating value) and returns its result in the representation res."] [186 1 "// cCallArgs calls f on ci's main thread."] [191 1 "// cNative makes hsi's C function fn at address a a native of ci's program: its arguments as the machine's values."] [196 1 "// cBridge makes f, a function of ci's program, call hsi's fn."] [220 1 "// cLabel is the address of the C program's object or function s, when it has one."] [234 1 "// cFlush flushes C's stdio at the program's end (libc's exit, after the Haskell handles' flush)."] [242 1 "// cValue is the value of the C program's object s in the representation res, when it has one: a capi import of a value"] [243 1 "// (foreign import capi \"h.h value i\"), whose wrapper GHC's C compiler makes and hsi reads as the object itself."] [267 1 "// identity is the word that stands for a heap object in memory C reads (an Array# argument's elements): a pinned byte"] [268 1 "// array's address, an integer itself, else an address of an unmapped region, one per object, kept for the run."] [293 1 "// identBase is the region of objects' identities: no mapping of crt's is there."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[50 20] [55 24] [57 29] [58 46] [59 26] [86 29] [91 34] [225 25] [228 43] [285 25]]} (go/file "cprog.go" :imports [


